            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The town of Goldhope had a small population in 1970, but the population has been increasing by a factor of 3 every decade since then.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p6-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "By what factor had the population increased from its 1970 value in 1980, 1990, 2000, 2010 and 2020?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "1980: $3$; 1990: $9$; 2000: $27$; 2010: $81$; 2020: $243$.",
          "worked": "Each decade contributes another factor of $3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{1980 factor}&=3^1=3\\\\\\text{1990 factor}&=3^2=9\\\\\\text{2000 factor}&=3^3=27\\\\\\text{2010 factor}&=3^4=81\\\\\\text{2020 factor}&=3^5=243\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "If the town’s population was $10\\,000$ in 1970, during which decade did the population pass $1\\,000\\,000$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "2010–2020.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Population in 2010}&=10\\,000\\times3^4=810\\,000\\\\\\text{Population in 2020}&=10\\,000\\times3^5=2\\,430\\,000\\end{align*}$$\nSince $810\\,000<1\\,000\\,000<2\\,430\\,000$, the population passed $1\\,000\\,000$ during 2010–2020.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      }
    ]
